  "query_preview": "(Today through Thursday)...\nIssued at 301 AM EDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nShowers will pass through the area this morning as a cold front \ndrops through the region, though disjointed and weakening upper \nlevel forcing has led to lighter amounts than previously expected.\n\nPrecip will gradually come to an end from northwest to southeast \nduring the day today, though trapped moisture below a low level \ninversion will keep the area cloudy much of the day. This along with \nthe low level cold advection behind the boundary will keep \ntemperatures from rising more than a few degrees today at most. \nSkies will clear out tonight, allowing lows to drop into the 40s \nacross the majority of the area.\n\nThe remainder of the forecast period will be dominated by two areas \nof surface high pressure, keeping temperatures near to below normal \nmuch of the weekend into early next week, and possibly providing an \nopportunity for the first patchy frost of the season next Monday \nnight, particularly if winds can go light to calm and allow lows to \ndrop even further than the current upper 30s across the northeastern \nportion of the area.\n\nSome recovery of temps mid to late week is expected with modestly \nrising heights aloft and southwesterly low level flow reestablishing \nitself on the backside of the second surface high, and temperatures \nmay creep back slightly above normal late week into next weekend for \na very pleasant stretch.",
